{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames","id":970447,"title":"Invisible Flames","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-15T20:34:07-07:00","id":970447,"title":"Invisible Flames","content":"Quick question, I know I know I ask a lot but hey, I love you guys.<br /> Ok so, is it possible to use prime 2, forces 4 and forces 2 to make a hugeass invisible fireball to burn down a forest for example? Yeah might need to find out if paradox will fuck me up or not too.<br /> EDIT: It's not a very large forest, I'd say it's 1-3 miles radius.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12133,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","user":"Leonardo","date":". 09-15-2016, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T20:57:31-07:00","id":970458,"title":"","content":"Not really. Perhaps Forces 3 Prime 2 and then Forces 4.<br /> Forces 3 and prime 2 to make fire out of nothing , then Forces 4 to grow the blaze into an inferno.<br /> <br /> It would be two seperate effects, take a tonne of successes, and be very dangerous to control. Fires like that can spread really easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:00:39-07:00","id":970460,"title":"","content":"Well, I'll PM you my idea cuz my community mates are watching my activities <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:03:54-07:00","id":970462,"title":"","content":"Can I ask if this is the plan to combat the Sept of Garou mentioned in other threads?<br /> <br /> Assuming this is related to the other threads you've started, that strategy is unlikely to work. I can elaborate more should you care.<br /> <br /> In any case, yes Paradox is going to be a bitch I would imagine. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12193_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12193\" data-vbnamecard=\"12193\">Saikou</a> stated that fire could be pretty hard to control for you, but that may not even matter if you aren't going to be on the ground there. The Effect does sound like it will take a decent amount of planning and successes to pull off. There are probably more efficient ways to accomplish what you intend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:35:58-07:00","id":970476,"title":"","content":"Considering that I've heard 'the invisible flame' as a nickname for hard radiation, an invisible burst of igniferous energy seems quite plausible as a potential effect. Unsure that Forces 4 is quite enough to get the magnitude of effect you seem to be looking for though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6072,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","user":"Quantumboost","date":". 09-16-2016, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:38:58-07:00","id":970477,"title":"","content":"More like covering the fireball with invisibility before it hits its target to make it as stealthy and undetected as possible before the impact, not trying to cloak it after the impact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T22:19:00-07:00","id":970491,"title":"","content":"That is impossible the way you wrote it.<br /> <br /> If you release the fireball AND want to make it invisible /before/ it hits the enemy, keep in mind the rule of 1 Arete roll per turn. The fireball will hit the target the same turn you casted it, unless you keep accumulating successes with +1 to difficulty penalty per additional turn of rolling, and that way you'll waste turns + your enemy will already see the fireball, clearly.<br /> <br /> Imagine it like this: you make fireball, release it and it flies to enemy. It will hit the same turn you made it. There's simply no time for you to do another Arete roll and cloak it, because rules disallow that you make more than 1 Arete roll during turn (exception: Wonders).<br /> <br /> Now, if you do plan to use Wonders, attacking with them still takes an action usually. Why? Because you need to aim your spell regardless, unless you want it to fly off randomly of course.<br /> <br /> However, it's all about wording.<br /> <br /> You cannot make separate Arete rolls for that, but you can split successes for that and basically do conjuctional magick (which people often forget about, oddly). But good luck with that, because you'd need at least --<br /> <br /> 1. 2+ successes for fireball, which would be only enough to affect it (affecting something or somebody else requires 2+ successes, as per M20). It would only increase difficulty to see your fireball by +2 (rules of invisibillity in How do you do that?)<br /> 2. Attacking successes, in case person will try to dodge + soak on top.<br /> 3. If you do extended rolls, cloaking is kinda useless. They've already seen it.<br /> <br /> Not really likely to happen in a single turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T22:22:06-07:00","id":970495,"title":"","content":"I was speaking about an ambush not combat situation, bogdan. I know I can't do it in combat, the whole purpose about it being invisible is not for combat and being in the sight of my enemy but more like ambushing them, pretty sure I'll have all the time I need to prepare it.<br /> Also about the fireball feat 1 success on arete is enough cuz forces grants +1 auto success anyway unless you fail of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T23:19:32-07:00","id":970525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leonardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames?p=970495#post970495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was speaking about an ambush not combat situation, bogdan. I know I can't do it in combat, the whole purpose about it being invisible is not for combat and being in the sight of my enemy but more like ambushing them, pretty sure I'll have all the time I need to prepare it.<br /> Also about the fireball feat 1 success on arete is enough cuz forces grants +1 auto success anyway unless you fail of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it's for ambush, go ahead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also about the fireball feat 1 success on arete is enough cuz forces grants +1 auto success anyway unless you fail of course. </div> </div> </div>Sigh. You missunderstood.<br /> <br /> It grants <i>damage</i> autosuccess, not casting autosuccess. Read M20 carefully.<br /> <br /> I'll give you a quick example.<br /> <br /> You use Forces to set someone ablaze, and you score 1 success. The spell failed, because you didn't score enough successes on casting, you need 2+.<br /> <br /> You use Forces to set someone ablaze, and you score 2 or more successes. And <i>on top of that, </i>you add <i>another</i> level of damage (as in, +1 damage autosuccess. Again, read carefully, <i>damage</i> autosuccess, not casting.)<br /> <br /> Quote from M20, page 515, Forces Sphere:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In game terms, Forces-based attacks inflict an additional<br /> <b><i>success of damage</i></b>. The nature of that damage depends upon<br /> the energies in question \u2013 see the Magickal Damage chart.<br /> Simple manifestations and manipulations are limited to the<br /> lower Sphere Ranks, whereas large-scale Effects demand higher<br /> levels of expertise. Most large Effects also demand plenty of<br /> successes and can become Paradox magnets for careless mages. </div> </div> </div>Another quote, page 504, Magickal Damage chart:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Magickal Damage<br /> <br /> \u2022 Bashing Damage: Mind Sphere Effects.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Lethal Damage: Most other Sphere Effects.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Aggravated Damage: Any Sphere when charged<br /> with Prime 2 and a point of Quintessence.<br /> Fire or electrical Forces Effects.<br /> Vulgar Entropy-, Life- or Prime-based Effects that directly<br /> disrupt the target\u2019s Pattern.<br /> <br /> Correspondence and Time inflict no damage unless they\u2019re<br /> combined with other Spheres.<br /> <br /> <b>The Forces Sphere adds one automatic success to Damage.</b><br /> <br /> Entropy inflicts damage only through indirect attacks until<br /> Rank 4; after that, damage is aggravated. </div> </div> </div>It is Damage autosuccess, not casting autosuccess, there's a big difference in that. Doing it the way you described is a great missuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T23:39:48-07:00","id":970532,"title":"","content":"I see, thanks for clearing that up, it would be much better if you didn't sigh at first <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> Could you give an example of how a ritual is done and such(talking about casting time triggers and estimated time between each roll to make them)? cuz you know how our community works and and how IC time differs from OOC time there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12133-leonardo","name":"Leonardo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T02:36:51-07:00","id":970586,"title":"","content":"What do you mean example of ritual?<br /> <br /> You have amount of rolls available equal to your Arete + Willpower.<br /> <br /> IC-wise, 1 Arete roll equals 1 IC hour of time. I personally see no need to wait OOCly as long as you elaborate what happens and that your character has spent time, but hey, I ain't the one to tell how server time stuff gonna work.<br /> <br /> You can do amount of rolls equal to your Stamina before you need to take a rest.<br /> <br /> You can spend Willpower point to put off ritual for later, take a rest and continue on (refreshes your Stamina). Difficulty to &quot;pick up&quot; the ritual from where you left is equal to base difficulty of the ritual (example: you want to ward something, the base difficulty was 8 before applying modifiers, that's your difficulty to pick it up again). You roll Wits + Esoterica to pick it up again. If you take a break again and then come back a second time to the same ritual, the difficulty to pick it up increases by +1, and it stacks endlessly for each time you come back to it.<br /> <br /> If you fail, that's it, you simply get no successes that turn, though you get +1 to difficulty for further rolls until you take a rest.<br /> <br /> If you botch -<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Botched Rolls<br /> <br /> If you roll a botch during a ritual, you may spend one turn,<br /> a temporary Willpower point, and one previously rolled success<br /> in order to keep the whole thing from blowing up in your face.<br /> At this point, your mage is holding the ritual together<br /> through sheer determination. You can either stop there or<br /> else keep going with a +1 increase to your difficulty. A second<br /> botch, however, spells immediate disaster\u2026 again, see Rituals<br /> and Paradox. </div> </div> </div>As for Paradox: if the ritual is vulgar, you get Paradox as usual, however for each additional roll you make you get another +1 to Paradox. If the ritual ends up botched or failed, it all comes down crushing on you. If ritual succeeded, you only take Paradox as usual, as from any other spell.<br /> <br /> If you're helped by unAwakened assistants (any human or other supernatural), you check &quot;Cult&quot; background for amount of people you need to get bonus dice to Arete rolls.<br /> <br /> If you're helped by Mages:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u2022 Equal Collaborators \u2013 that is, mages who are more or less<br /> on the same level as the primary caster \u2013 can roll their<br /> Arete and then add their successes toward the success<br /> of the ritual as a whole. The Effect\u2019s normal difficulty<br /> and modifiers apply equally to all such collaborators.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Enlightened assistants \u2013 that is, mages with less knowledge<br /> and experience than the primary caster \u2013 add one<br /> automatic success to the Effect, up to a maximum of<br /> five successes, total. These successes, however, DO NOT<br /> APPLY to cancel out a botch. If the caster botches the roll,<br /> then those assistants\u2019 successes disappear. The additional<br /> successes count only to enhance a successful Effect.<br /> Only one option may be used at a time \u2013 not both. </div> </div> </div>All Spheres must match if Mages are of less expertise. (example: you do warding with Correspondence, Life and Prime. There's two mages, one with Correspondence/ Life/ Prime, and another with only Correspondence and Prime. The one with three Spheres just like you can help. If their Sphere ranks are equal to yours, see &quot;Equal Collaborators&quot;). Mages who try to help you must have matching Paradigms and Focus, else they get penalties (or are unable to help at all).<br /> <br /> If you're interrupted during ritual (fight occurs, someone tries to tackle you down, that sort of thing), you must roll Willpower at difficulty of 8. If you fail - it's all gone and treat it as botching magick, Paradox blows up in your face. If you succeed - treat it as botch during ritual, aka you get +1 to difficulty until you take a rest and next botch or interferance will put it down for good.<br /> <br /> <br /> That's pretty much all you need to know about rituals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:38:14-07:00","id":970683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bogdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames?p=970491#post970491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unless you keep accumulating successes with +1 to difficulty penalty per additional turn of rolling</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait... This is a thing? I have been looking for something like this, but have been unsuccessful. Do you remember where in the extremely heavy PDF this is mentioned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:51:32-07:00","id":970690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames?p=970683#post970683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait... This is a thing? I have been looking for something like this, but have been unsuccessful. Do you remember where in the extremely heavy PDF this is mentioned?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's been a thing since Revised at least (can't speak for 2nd). I find this rule to be really harsh for Mages with Arete 5 or less, so I usually augment it so augmented Arete rolls only increase in diffulcty after 10 successes have been reached. However, fails will always increase the difficulty.<br /> <br /> That's kind the reason why Rituals are a thing, to get around this increase in difficulty for big flashy spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:53:32-07:00","id":970692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames?p=970683#post970683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait... This is a thing? I have been looking for something like this, but have been unsuccessful. Do you remember where in the extremely heavy PDF this is mentioned?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Here.<br /> <br /> M20, page 537, the bottom of the page.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Picking Up Where You Left Off<br /> <br /> After casting an imperfect Effect or falling short of her initial<br /> plans, a mage can pick up where she left off by making another<br /> roll at +1 to the original difficulty. In story terms, she grits her<br /> teeth, regroups, and gives it the old (wizard) college try once again. </div> </div> </div>If you ever want to stack successes, here's how it goes down:<br /> <br /> 1. You do a ritual and follow the rules of ritual. (Usually, it's 1 hour per 1 Arete roll. Definitely not for combat or quick action)<br /> 2. You do turn-to-turn rolling, but each new turn you keep rolling you get +1 to base difficulty, which you cannot modify and thus reduce. Surely you won't stack as many successes as you could with ritual, but it's good for quick action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12132-bogdan","name":"Bogdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:54:52-07:00","id":970693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames?p=970683#post970683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait... This is a thing? I have been looking for something like this, but have been unsuccessful. Do you remember where in the extremely heavy PDF this is mentioned?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mage 20, page 537 'Picking up where you left off' goes 'After casting an imperfect Effect or falling short of her initial plans, a mage can pick up where she left off by making another roll at +1 to the original difficulty'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames?p=970690#post970690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been a thing since Revised at least (can't speak for 2nd). I find this rule to be really harsh for Mages with Arete 5 or less, so I usually augment it so augmented Arete rolls only increase in diffulcty after 10 successes have been reached. However, fails will always increase the difficulty.</div> </div> </div> </div>When using Revised, that definitely makes sense. Revised has very high demands when it comes to the amount of successes needed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T08:05:06-07:00","id":970700,"title":"","content":"Technically the martian heat ray from war of the world's was both invisible and silent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T11:34:30-07:00","id":970801,"title":"","content":"Can't you just make an invisible fire? Like increasing the area heat absurdly to catch fire in the trees? This way it doesn't requires 2 Arete rolls and might be coincident. Also, will ambush everyone. An increase that really burns people would be vulgar, though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:25:54-07:00","id":970830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> M20, page 537 </div> </div> </div>I have no idea how I overlooked that... multiple times. I was trying to figure out how that kind of thing could work. so would each roll require a Q to keep fueling it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:46:15-07:00","id":970843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>frostbyte000jm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames?p=970830#post970830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea how I overlooked that... multiple times. I was trying to figure out how that kind of thing could work. so would each roll require a Q to keep fueling it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whee does that section mention Quintessence? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Just keep increasing the difficulty by +1 with each roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:48:03-07:00","id":970846,"title":"","content":"Okay, by the way, since the invisible fire keeps coming up...here is how to make invisible fire:<br /> <br /> Step 1: Create an orb of intense heat and toss it<br /> Step 2: There is no step 2.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:59:42-07:00","id":970856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames?p=970843#post970843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whee does that section mention Quintessence?.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll start a new topic. I don't think I have seen one yet about Q amounts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2900-frostbyte000jm","name":"frostbyte000jm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:19:42-07:00","id":973797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leonardo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames#post970447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question, I know I know I ask a lot but hey, I love you guys.<br /> Ok so, is it possible to use prime 2, forces 4 and forces 2 to make a hugeass invisible fireball to burn down a forest for example? Yeah might need to find out if paradox will fuck me up or not too.<br /> EDIT: It's not a very large forest, I'd say it's 1-3 miles radius.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> why? Just use forces 3 or forces 2 (depending on scale) to manipulate heat. It's completely invisible and mostly coincidental. I mean you could literally burn someone to ashes just by looking at them and claim spontaneous combustion, less said about starting a fire the best. You can even kill someone with forces 2 by manipulating body temperature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T17:53:53-07:00","id":974143,"title":"","content":"Yep, so long as its something your Paradigm allows for Invisible Fire can totally be a thing in a single effect. Possibly less likely in the hands of a Hermetic or Chorister and more likely from an Etherites Ray Gun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T18:42:48-07:00","id":974169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames?p=973797#post973797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why? Just use forces 3 or forces 2 (depending on scale) to manipulate heat. It's completely invisible and mostly coincidental. I mean you could literally burn someone to ashes just by looking at them and claim spontaneous combustion, less said about starting a fire the best. You can even kill someone with forces 2 by manipulating body temperature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just my opinion, but cooking someone from the inside is not coincidental (under any sort of normal circumstances). Spontaneous combustion is not a thing that people in general are going to accept. &quot;Whoops, he instantly burnt to a crisp. Nothing weird there.&quot; is not going to happen.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T04:56:05-07:00","id":974336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames?p=974169#post974169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just my opinion, but cooking someone from the inside is not coincidental (under any sort of normal circumstances). Spontaneous combustion is not a thing that people in general are going to accept. &quot;Whoops, he instantly burnt to a crisp. Nothing weird there.&quot; is not going to happen.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> oh of course no, you are correct... to a point. seeing soneone on fire wouldn't instantly trigger cognitive dissonance, it may have any number of rational explanations, for an example if the guy is on a gas station, smoking or something like that.<br /> Also, while I admit that pointing a wand at someone and setting them on fire is vulgar, if the said person burns to ashes in his bedroom with no witnesses, it's a Spontaneous Combustion.<br /> On the other head such measures would be more effective against supernaturally tough opponents, like a massively augmented androids, vampires and the like. You can simply and coincidentally give someone a stroke, brain aneurism and such with low level Forces, internal organs are very temperature sensitive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T06:31:46-07:00","id":974371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames?p=974336#post974336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, while I admit that pointing a wand at someone and setting them on fire is vulgar, if the said person burns to ashes in his bedroom with no witnesses, it's a Spontaneous Combustion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using the Spontaneous Combustion reasoning, wouldn't that just make it Vulgar <i>without witnesses</i>?(except under specific circumstances where the consensus would consider it coincidental, like the gas station setup above). So a coincidental burning to death in a bedroom would have to happen (for example) by having an outlet short out and catch fire. If you just magically apply fire directly to body and have the person die, that seems fairly Vulgar (this is actually a question, not a statement).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames?p=974336#post974336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On the other head such measures would be more effective against supernaturally tough opponents, like a massively augmented androids, vampires and the like. You can simply and coincidentally give someone a stroke, brain aneurism and such with low level Forces, internal organs are very temperature sensitive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think just having people drop dead falls pretty near the circumstances above. It is either Vulgar to start, or becomes Vulgar very very quickly (by the second person?).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T08:58:08-07:00","id":974442,"title":"","content":"People drop dead for no apparent reason all the time. Heart attacks, strokes, poison, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4259-eddie-fiori","name":"Eddie Fiori","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T09:36:53-07:00","id":974469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames?p=974336#post974336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> oh of course no, you are correct... to a point. seeing soneone on fire wouldn't instantly trigger cognitive dissonance, it may have any number of rational explanations, for an example if the guy is on a gas station, smoking or something like that.<br /> Also, while I admit that pointing a wand at someone and setting them on fire is vulgar, if the said person burns to ashes in his bedroom with no witnesses, it's a Spontaneous Combustion.<br /> On the other head such measures would be more effective against supernaturally tough opponents, like a massively augmented androids, vampires and the like. You can simply and coincidentally give someone a stroke, brain aneurism and such with low level Forces, internal organs are very temperature sensitive.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what Life 3 is for, if you want Forces on top it is your choice.<br /> But Forces alone to give someone an aneurism is not going to fly at most tables.<br /> Likewise # of successes:<br /> To give someone a fatal heart attack demands at least 4 successes for dealing 8 damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T09:40:50-07:00","id":974472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames?p=974469#post974469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is what Life 3 is for, if you want Forces on top it is your choice.<br /> But Forces alone to give someone an aneurism is not going to fly at most tables.<br /> Likewise # of successes:<br /> To give someone a fatal heart attack demands at least 4 successes for dealing 8 damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>^this. That's pretty much how I see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T11:54:29-07:00","id":974567,"title":"","content":"Worth noting that even if you <i>do</i> rule Spontaneous Unexplainable Combustion as Coincidental, doing it too <i>often</i> means you're dealing with the Domino Effect, which pushes things into Vulgar. Reality baselines apply to more than just individual events.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T00:42:15-07:00","id":975412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames?p=974469#post974469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is what Life 3 is for, if you want Forces on top it is your choice.<br /> But Forces alone to give someone an aneurism is not going to fly at most tables.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> and if you don't have Life? I do know some effects can be achieved with multiple arcana. For example you could rise body temperature using Life, without Forces.<br /> <br /> Tempereture manipulation is forces, effects of extreme temp. can be googled in seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","user":"Warpwind","date":". 09-24-2016, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T03:43:01-07:00","id":975458,"title":"","content":"If you rise the temperature in the vincinity (sp?) or to create a bubble of heated air around someone. But to lock it you need Life again.<br /> But rising the body temperature directly is impossible with forces alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T04:51:37-07:00","id":975471,"title":"","content":"I never liked this whole &quot;lock it into the pattern&quot; thing M20 introduced. It makes Life become essential to do anything on people.<br /> <br /> It makes the Hermetic Force rotes like the Friction Curse need Life, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T09:23:40-07:00","id":975552,"title":"","content":"I think you only need to lock if you want it to be persistent wherever the target go. For a instant effect like this, there is no need to lock, so Forces alone is enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T09:51:16-07:00","id":975566,"title":"","content":"Yes. Locking is only necessary if you are doing an effect that would normalyl be usable on a location, and you want to lock it to move along with another pattern. The given example is invisibility by bending light. You are essentially creating a field that shows nothing inside it, but in order to have it move with a person instead of just sitting in a place, you lock it onto that person with Life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T11:37:10-07:00","id":975622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/970447-invisible-flames?p=975566#post975566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Locking is only necessary if you are doing an effect that would normalyl be usable on a location, and you want to lock it to move along with another pattern. The given example is invisibility by bending light. You are essentially creating a field that shows nothing inside it, but in order to have it move with a person instead of just sitting in a place, you lock it onto that person with Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>What happens if you Lock the effect on to your own kinetic energy or body heat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]}